
2
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:05,790
911. What's your emergency?

3
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:07,910
Hello?

4
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,040
This is 911. Go ahead.

5
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:16,660
This is Suh Young-chul, who used to work at Chains Bio.

6
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,790
Today at the Doongwoori Building I plan to run an experiment.

7
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,870
Excuse me? Can you repeat that, please?

8
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:27,200
Ah, not an experiment.

9
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,910
It's closer to terrorism.

10
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:29,910
What?

11
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:34,910
That's right. A highly contagious bioterror attack.

12
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:41,410
I tested the pathogen in my body.

13
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:49,910
And it was a success.

14
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:55,450
I am the only vaccine that can stop this outbreak.

15
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,910
Organisms of the same species that,

16
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:03,160
for a certain time, live in the same place

17
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:19,040
Why are you waiting for me?

18
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,200
You're 10 minutes late. What was it this time?

19
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,500
It was nothing.

20
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:26,370
Traffic was bad,

21
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:28,790
so the taxi driver tried to let me off across the street.

22
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:29,580
So ?

23
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:32,950
Yeah, these things happen.

24
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:37,080
It's okay if I say it, but how can he say that to me?

25
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,200
So ?

26
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:41,750
It's not what I wanted.

27
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,700
I said, however long it takes,

28
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,620
drop me off at the spot I chose.

29
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,160
What?

30
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:53,790
So it's my fault again?

31
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,160
Welcome to the Chains Blo Conference,

32
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,580
a leading platform for future technology.

33
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,660
Thank you.

34
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:02,040
You brought the invitation I gave you?

35
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,450
...and now we'll hear from CEO Kang Woo-cheol.

36
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,330
Please give him a round of applause.

37
00:03:13,410 --> 00:03:14,290
Is that the guy?

38
00:03:14,290 --> 00:03:16,910
The one I should grovel to if I want to work here?

39
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,700
If only you got along with your dean,

40
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,700
this wouldn't be necessary.

41
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,080
Sure, my fault again.

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,750
But don't you care how that dean

43
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,410
treated his graduate students?

44
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:31,830
No, I don't.

45
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:34,700
Well, I'm sure he's a jerk.

46
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,830
And you couldn't tolerate that.

47
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,910
So you got on his bad side, and didn't get reappointed.

48
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:44,750
I'm just curious...

49
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:47,540
Why are you so fixated on your ex-wife's career

50
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:48,910
10 years after the divorce?

51
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,370
Because you have no friends.

52
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:56,000
You keep doing things that make people hate you.

53
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,450
Does your wife know you look after your ex-wife like this?

54
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:02,000
My wife is not as sensitive as you are.

55
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,580
She's probably even concerned for you.

56
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:06,540
What a cool wife.

57
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,870
You're a great match. I'm happy for you.

58
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,620
If I say our company's main business

59
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,620
is collective intelligence,

60
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:16,120
people might wonder,

61
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:17,660
"Why is a bio company,

62
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:20,830
rather than an IT company, studying that topic?"

63
00:04:21,330 --> 00:04:24,000
Collective intelligence is a common term

64
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,830
in the field of sociology,

65
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
but the first person to use the term

66
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:32,000
was an entomologist who studied ants,

67
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,870
William Morton Wheeler.

68
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:37,410
Collective intelligence is a key force driving evolution.

69
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,910
You know the yellow slime mold 'Physarum polycephalum'?

70
00:04:41,330 --> 00:04:43,000
These fellows upgrade themselves

71
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,500
through information exchange

72
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:47,700
and optimize the direction of their growth towards food.

73
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,200
Although not multicellular organisms,

74
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,790
they can learn and remember.

75
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,790
Inspired by these remarkable traits,

76
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:56,540
we were able to dramatically improve

77
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,620
the production of organic semiconductors.

78
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,620
Let's give a hand to our little collaborators.

79
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:08,160
This guy's more interesting than I expected.

80
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:11,250
This isn't some lame company that makes copycat drugs.

81
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:13,370
It's a serious, enterprising firm.

82
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:15,200
After I introduced you,

83
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,410
they even sent another invitation for you.

84
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:20,540
Actually, that's why I came.

85
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,830
I was curious what this message meant.

86
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,910
To Prof. Kwon: Imperfect communication,

87
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,200
the source of all tragedy

88
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:30,540
...so this chip helps damaged nerves carry information.

89
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:34,290
We injected it into a rat with severed spinal nerves

90
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:36,080
and paralyzed hind legs,

91
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:39,870
and as you can see, just a moment later,

92
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:43,500
It was able to move no different from a healthy rat.

93
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,750
If we continue with this research,

94
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,080
and apply it to the human brain,

95
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:58,410
I believe it may enable a direct transfer

96
00:05:58,450 --> 00:06:01,200
of information between individuals.

97
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:03,620
When that happens,

98
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,790
we may live in a world where

99
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:09,000
you can't think bad thoughts in front of others.

100
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,410
Thank you, CEO Kang.

101
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,040
Please give him a round of applause!

102
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:25,000
Next, to introduce Chains Bio's global market strategy...

103
00:06:32,330 --> 00:06:34,290
It's your first vacation in ages.

104
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:38,160
So why spend it with the younger brother you see every day?

105
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:42,500
This way I can get some fresh air, go shopping...

106
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:44,910
You know how stifling it is working at a computer all day?

107
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:53,540
Wow, look at all the camping stuff they have these days.

108
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,330
I could just live outdoors.

109
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,040
The clothes are nice, too.

110
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,330
Should we go camping? On your next vacation?

111
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,410
-The two of us? - Yeah, let's go.

112
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,040
We'll grill some meat...

113
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,790
That'd be great!

114
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:10,910
We can go, why not?

115
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:13,500
That's great. I'll buy some equipment. SECURITY

116
00:07:14,250 --> 00:07:16,620
You get back to work. Lunchtime will end soon.

117
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:19,450
- No, I'll head back after you. - No need.

118
00:07:19,450 --> 00:07:22,160
The facilities here are great. So convenient.

119
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:27,330
Don't I work my ass off so I can live in civilization?

120
00:07:27,330 --> 00:07:29,580
You always go on about civilization,

121
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,500
why do you want to go camping?

122
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,160
Camping is civilization, too.

123
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,290
Go on. See you at home.

124
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,120
I'll look around before going.

125
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,160
Selamat tinggal.

126
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:39,370
-Take care..- Yeah.

127
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:40,910
Take care. Yeah.

128
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:47,410
Hello, sir. I enjoyed your presentation.

129
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:49,120
Oh, Professor Han.

130
00:07:49,330 --> 00:07:52,700
This is Professor Kwon Se-jeong, who I mentioned last time.

131
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:54,500
Thank you for inviting me.

132
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:57,120
And for this note on my invitation.

133
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,330
Just a moment.

134
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,250
Hello?

135
00:08:01,410 --> 00:08:02,500
Mr. Kang Woo-cheol?

136
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,750
Yes. Who's speaking?

137
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:07,540
I'm Lee Bong-seok, from the Seoul Counterterrorism Squad.

138
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:08,950
How can I help you?

139
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,830
You know a man named Suh Young-chul?

140
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:14,250
This call seems important. Let's talk later.

141
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:16,330
Ah, sure. We'll wait.

142
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:22,000
You sure he's the one who sent this invitation?

143
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,830
What are you doing? Go after him.

144
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:24,540
What?

145
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,330
Just hand him your card

146
00:08:26,370 --> 00:08:29,620
and say "I'm Kwon Se-jeong," that's all. ,

147
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:40,080
Why are you looking for Dr. Suh?

148
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:41,330
We received a call

149
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:43,620
that Dr. Suh is planning a terrorist attack

150
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:45,830
in the building hosting your conference.

151
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,500
I think I saw him today at the conference.

152
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,660
Are you certain?

153
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:53,750
Not 100% certain.

154
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,500
He was standing too far away.

155
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:58,080
Our team will arrive there soon.

156
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,330
If you see him again, call me immediately at this number.

157
00:09:00,330 --> 00:09:01,700
All right, I will.

158
00:09:27,450 --> 00:09:29,120
Nice speech, Woo-cheol.

159
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,830
So impressive.

160
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:33,830
Information exchange through organic semiconductors?

161
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:38,580
You know how hard I researched that.

162
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:42,080
Consciousness in a multilateral network.

163
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,500
Well, if that existed,

164
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:49,120
no one would be betrayed and kicked out like me, right?

165
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,830
You freak.

166
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:55,540
The technology you researched can't be used anywhere.

167
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:57,870
Bro.

168
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:01,950
I'm taking humanity to the next level.

169
00:10:03,410 --> 00:10:05,910
Enabling a second cognitive revolution.

170
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,290
You know what?

171
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:14,000
You...

172
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,950
are just a psycho.

173
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:19,580
Get lost, you loser!

174
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,450
But when you hired me,

175
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:29,290
you said my research was great.

176
00:10:29,450 --> 00:10:31,540
That you respected my research.

177
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:36,660
It was all just an act, so you could steal my research.

178
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,410
And now... psycho?

179
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:42,580
You stole research from that psycho.

180
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:47,870
You just want to make humans go extinct, don't you?

181
00:10:48,830 --> 00:10:50,500
Not extinct.

182
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:51,950
It's a birth.

183
00:10:52,370 --> 00:10:53,950
The birth of a new humanity.

184
00:10:54,370 --> 00:10:55,910
Just imagine it.

185
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,580
Perfect communication will be possible.

186
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:01,410
All the byproducts of crass individualism,

187
00:11:01,450 --> 00:11:03,410
jealousy, rivalry, suspicion...

188
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:08,620
Those bizarre losses that arise from unstable communication.

189
00:11:08,950 --> 00:11:10,830
That's what I'm trying to stop.

190
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:15,370
Wow!

191
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,750
You crazy freak.

192
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,580
Give it a try.

193
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:25,290
It's got nothing to do with me.

194
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:28,370
I'm clocking out, so good luck with that.

195
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:34,540
I want you to be the link between me and the new humanity.

196
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,540
What the hell are you doing?

197
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:43,830
Research.

198
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,200
You goddamned maniac!

199
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,330
Hey, look at this.

200
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:29,830
Hey mister!

201
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:31,410
Shouldn't we call 911?

202
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:51,580
Did you talk to him?

203
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,540
Seemed like a bad time.

204
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:57,540
Really? Just a sec.

205
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:02,370
No, really. I don't think he'll want to talk now.

206
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:11,370
Let's go eat. He'll call back.

207
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,160
Police. Where's the conference hall?

208
00:13:26,290 --> 00:13:28,790
Turn left and go up the stairs, then...

209
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:34,750
What is that?

210
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:39,580
Go.

211
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:42,290
Sir, are you okay?

212
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:49,750
Call the containment team. - What?

213
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:51,080
Call for a lockdown!

214
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:00,750
Hi!

215
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:03,250
Where are you, Daddy? What are you doing?

216
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:05,080
I'll head home now.

217
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,540
Honey, where's your passport?

218
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,910
Should be in the drawer in the study.

219
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,580
- You still with Professor Kwon? - Yeah.

220
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:15,040
I'll head home soon.

221
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,540
Want to say hi?

222
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,000
Anyway, hurry home. We need to pack.

223
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:22,870
Okay.

224
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:25,500
Say bye to Dad. - Hurry home, Dad!

225
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:28,410
Where are you going? Traveling?

226
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:35,160
Why don't you answer? You immigrating or something?

227
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,080
Well...

228
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,160
A teaching position opened at UC Irvine...

229
00:14:40,410 --> 00:14:43,450
Really, you're going to the US? For how long?

230
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,830
This time, we may just stay there.

231
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:56,410
Ah, now I get it.

232
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,080
You're leaving, so you wanted to set

233
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:01,450
your ex-wife up with a job before going?

234
00:15:02,410 --> 00:15:03,660
Anyway, congrats.

235
00:15:03,790 --> 00:15:05,410
It's good news, right?

236
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:11,080
Since it's the last time, let me ask.

237
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:14,330
Why did you marry me?

238
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:19,500
Well...

239
00:15:20,370 --> 00:15:23,910
The way you never back down when you think you're right...

240
00:15:23,910 --> 00:15:25,540
your personality?

241
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:29,250
Wow, after you always begged me not to do that.

242
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,870
You liked that?

243
00:15:32,290 --> 00:15:35,080
I did... I liked it.

244
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,830
But I couldn't keep up with you.

245
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,250
I couldn't handle it.

246
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:43,450
I've always been a bit of a coward.

247
00:15:44,870 --> 00:15:47,080
That's why I broke up with you.

248
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:53,450
Don't worry. I'll be okay.

249
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:57,200
It's not like you, talking like that.

250
00:15:58,250 --> 00:15:59,580
I'm not saying you should change...

251
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:00,660
Done eating?

252
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,450
Let's go, your wife is waiting.

253
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:05,910
There she goes again....

254
00:16:10,450 --> 00:16:11,450
Thank you.

255
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:14,870
Have a good evening.

256
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,870
Welcome.

257
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,830
Shit, that's so funny. Yeah...

258
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:22,790
Hey, I'll call you back.

259
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,700
I'm gonna stuff my face.

260
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:25,790
Yeah.

261
00:16:28,370 --> 00:16:30,160
Three people? - Yes, three.

262
00:16:30,330 --> 00:16:34,120
From here to here....we'll take it all.

263
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,250
All of it?

264
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:36,830
Yeah, all of it.

265
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:44,120
You're paying today.

266
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:45,790
Faham Got it?

267
00:16:49,370 --> 00:16:51,290
Damn it, So-eun!

268
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,330
You should answer him, huh?

269
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,700
The entire building is being locked down.

270
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:03,580
Security personnel, evacuate everyone immediately!

271
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:05,620
What's going on?

272
00:17:09,450 --> 00:17:10,330
Hey!

273
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:19,450
Everyone evacuate!

274
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:21,160
Move! Out of the way!

275
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,540
Come out! Everyone move!

276
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,200
Isn't the parking lot that way?

277
00:17:38,330 --> 00:17:39,410
Se-jeong.

278
00:17:41,370 --> 00:17:45,290
You should find at least one friend you can rely on.

279
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:51,830
Everyone run!

280
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,290
Run!

281
00:18:12,870 --> 00:18:13,910
Se-jeong!

282
00:18:14,370 --> 00:18:15,410
Damn it...

283
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,290
Hurry!

284
00:18:57,450 --> 00:18:58,410
That way!

285
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,790
Come quick! Hurry!

286
00:19:34,330 --> 00:19:36,580
Hyun-hee, are you hurt?

287
00:19:37,290 --> 00:19:39,080
I'm okay.

288
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:43,040
What's going on?

289
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:45,870
It's a terrorist attack.

290
00:19:46,750 --> 00:19:48,040
Who are you?

291
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:49,580
I'm a policeman.

292
00:19:49,870 --> 00:19:51,870
We got a call that a bioterrorist attack

293
00:19:51,870 --> 00:19:53,660
